For a point over an element with no line near it, Ladybird’s
caretPositionFromPoint() now returns the position at that
element’s start rather than null, as Blink, WebKit and Gecko
all do. Blink’s LayoutBlockFlow::PositionForPoint() returns
CreatePositionWithAffinity(0) for a block without fragments; WebKit’s
RenderBlockFlow::positionForPointWithInlineChildren() returns
createPositionWithAffinity(0) when InlineIterator::firstLineBoxFor()
finds no line; and Gecko’s nsIFrame::GetContentOffsetsFromPoint() falls
back to OffsetsForSingleFrame(), which gives the frame’s content range.
None of them returns null over an element.
